    {
      "id": 68,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        820
      ],
      "size": [
        500,
        470
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Read me - speed, settings, prompt tips + low VRAM",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Speed (tested, RTX 4000 Ada 20 GB, int8 set)\n- **Use PyTorch for CUDA 13 (cu130).** On CUDA 12.8 it was about 3.5x slower.\n- 8 MP image: ~30 s sampling (4 MP ~12 s, 16 MP ~86 s). Prompt upsampler: ~10-15 s.\n\n## Settings (official, already set)\n8 steps (Manual Sigmas), euler, no CFG (Basic Guider), sigma shift 1 / 1.\n\n## Prompt tips\n- **Prompt upsampler on:** one line is enough, it writes the full prompt. Keep the aspect ratio in **Upsampler input** the same as in **Size**.\n- **Off (exact details):** your prompt goes to the model as written. Plain sentences: the camera and lens, the light and where it comes from, no hype words (ultra detailed, masterpiece). Put text in \"quotes\".\n- A result misses? Try it the other way, it's another ~30 s.\n- **Image Scale By** doubles the saved image (lanczos). Set it to 1 to save at 8 MP.\n\n## Low VRAM (tested by capping the VRAM on a 20 GB card)\n- Load the w4a8 model and the w4a8 text encoder: full speed at an 8 GB and a 6 GB cap.\n- At the 6 GB cap 4 MP peaked at ~5.3 GB but 8 MP at ~8.1 GB, so use 4 MP on a 6 GB card.\n- The prompt upsampler slows to ~30-50 s under a cap. ComfyUI used up to ~17.5 GB of system RAM."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Speed (tested, RTX 4000 Ada 20 GB, int8 set)\n- **Use PyTorch for CUDA 13 (cu130).** On CUDA 12.8 it was about 3.5x slower.\n- 8 MP image: ~30 s sampling (4 MP ~12 s, 16 MP ~86 s). Prompt upsampler: ~10-15 s.\n\n## Settings (official, already set)\n8 steps (Manual Sigmas), euler, no CFG (Basic Guider), sigma shift 1 / 1.\n\n## Prompt tips\n- **Prompt upsampler on:** one line is enough, it writes the full prompt. Keep the aspect ratio in **Upsampler input** the same as in **Size**.\n- **Off (exact details):** your prompt goes to the model as written. Plain sentences: the camera and lens, the light and where it comes from, no hype words (ultra detailed, masterpiece). Put text in \"quotes\".\n- A result misses? Try it the other way, it's another ~30 s.\n- **Image Scale By** doubles the saved image (lanczos). Set it to 1 to save at 8 MP.\n\n## Low VRAM (tested by capping the VRAM on a 20 GB card)\n- Load the w4a8 model and the w4a8 text encoder: full speed at an 8 GB and a 6 GB cap.\n- At the 6 GB cap 4 MP peaked at ~5.3 GB but 8 MP at ~8.1 GB, so use 4 MP on a 6 GB card.\n- The prompt upsampler slows to ~30-50 s under a cap. ComfyUI used up to ~17.5 GB of system RAM."
      },
